hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20885","Waki' narrated to me, Qurrah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal al-Adawi, from a man among them called Khalid ibn Umayr, then Abu Na'amah said: I heard it from Khalid ibn Umayr, he said: Utbah ibn Ghazwan preached to us, Abu Na'amah said: On the pulpit, and Qurrah did not say it, so he said: Indeed the world has announced its end and turned away swiftly, and nothing remains of it except a remnant like the remnant of a vessel, and you are in a house soon to move from it, so move with the best of what is present with you, for I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we had no food to eat except tree leaves, until our mouth corners were sore. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I heard my father say: None narrated this hadith except Waki', meaning it is rare."
"20886","Isma'il narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from a man, Ayyub said: I think it is Khalid ibn Umayr, he said: I heard Utbah ibn Ghazwan preaching, then he mentioned the hadith, he said: And I saw myself as the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or he said: Among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we had no food except trees, or he said: Tree leaves, until our mouth corners were sore. My father said: This Abu Na'amah is Amr ibn Isa, and Abu Na'amah al-Sa'di is another, older than this, and this one is older than that one."
"20887","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Agharr, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from his grandfather Qays ibn Asim, that he accepted Islam, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to wash with water and lote."
